    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup is anchored by the dual-threat upside of **Lawrence Butler** (70.35) and **Taylor Ward** (69.90), both of whom benefit from favorable matchups against moderate pitching and significant park factor boosts. **Lawrence Butler** is our standout play, leveraging an elite platoon advantage against Melton that pushes his score well into the 70s. Similarly, **Taylor Ward** and **Dylan Beavers** (69.52) are prime targets; both players are enjoying a 16% park-factor surge today, neutralizing any concerns regarding the opposing arm, Rea. While **Dylan Beavers** faces a slight penalty for the catcher's ability to suppress stolen bases, his high-efficiency profile makes him a core component of our aggressive SB strategy.\n\nThe decision to bench **Jung Hoo Lee** (43.94) and **JJ Bleday** (43.72) was a razor-thin margin, with both players failing to clear the higher threshold established by our middle-order bats. **Jung Hoo Lee** was the closest to cracking the utility spot, but his lower projection relative to **Jonathan Aranda** (56.90)\u2014who benefits from a +12% dynamic platoon boost against Cole\u2014pushed him to the pine. We are also monitoring the matchup for **Luis Arraez** (42.76) and **Masyn Winn** (42.79); despite their lower scores, we are deploying them for their consistent contact profiles, though we remain wary of the strikeout potential posed by Cease and Harrison, respectively.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given the elite arms on the slate. **Bryce Harper** (57.65) faces a stiff test against Burns, yet his elite xwOBA of 0.404 and the benefit of leading off keep his floor stable. **Daulton Varsho** (54.09) is a marginal start against the efficiency of Webb, and we are proceeding with caution regarding **Cal Raleigh** (65.29) and **Gavin Sheets** (63.23), both of whom are projected to deliver strong value despite moderate park environments. Ensure all daily caps are monitored, as **Tyler Freeman** remains sidelined and unavailable to provide coverage should any late-inning tactical substitutions be required.",
